  <item>
    <title>Ep.01 读书而已，just for fun</title>
    <link>https://www.xiaoyuzhoufm.com/episode/63079139ea3aed95e5336b48</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">63079139ea3aed95e5336b48</guid>
    <pubDate>Thu, 25 Aug 2022 15:11:52 +0000</pubDate>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><strong><span>Show notes:</span></strong></p><span></span><p><strong><span>【本期讲述】</span></strong></p><span></span><p><span>本期聊聊[读书]，不知道读书在你人生中充当着什么样的位置？本期节目将从“我与阅读的关系”、“阅读洗礼后的变化”、“读书的深层领悟”、“后续知识变现”四个大方面分别分享对其的看法。我们表达的只不过是自己长期阅读后的感受，重要的是下落地球那天的你仍然可保持体系性知识的渴望，不断地学习，不要放弃自己的可塑性。</span></p><span></span><p><span>如果听众们有不同意见欢迎评论和投稿告诉我们。</span></p><span></span><p><strong><span>You might get：</span></strong></p><span></span><ul><span>  </span><li><span>把《生命不能承受之轻》当小黄书看</span></li><span>  </span><li><span>阅读让我逃离现实生活而已</span></li><span>  </span><li><span>书看多了，我觉得大家都是傻逼</span></li><span>  </span><li><span>虽然读书好处很多，但也绝对不鼓吹大家读书</span></li><span>  </span><li><span>读书的价值没有从[表面]体现不代表读书没用</span></li><span>  </span><li><span>有了独立思考去对抗世界的逆流</span></li><span>  </span><li><span>我是个读书的人同时也是个满嘴脏话的人</span></li><span>  </span><li><span>互联网让更多的人阅读了</span></li><span>  </span><li><span>碎片式信息断送知识形成网格</span></li><span></span></ul><span></span><p><strong><span>【本期提及】</span></strong></p><span></span><p><a href="http://m.zwbk.org/lemma/96251" data-url="http://m.zwbk.org/lemma/96251"><span>严歌苓简介</span></a></p><span></span><p><a href="https://www.ted.com/talks/adam_grant_how_to_stop_languishing_and_start_finding_flow" data-url="https://www.ted.com/talks/adam_grant_how_to_stop_languishing_and_start_finding_flow"><span>TED演讲 How to stop languishing and start finding flow：</span></a></p><span></span><p><a href="https://book.douban.com/subject/1017143/" data-url="https://book.douban.com/subject/1017143/"><span>《不能承受的生命之轻》</span></a></p><span></span><p><a href="https://podcaster.xiaoyuzhoufm.com/podcasts/61473dd3e6868572bfc88ca8/63079139ea3aed95e5336b48/%C2%A0https://book.douban.com/subject/26285299/" data-url="https://podcaster.xiaoyuzhoufm.com/podcasts/61473dd3e6868572bfc88ca8/63079139ea3aed95e5336b48/%C2%A0https://book.douban.com/subject/26285299/"><span>《创造力:心流与创新心理学》&nbsp;</span></a></p><span></span><p><a href="https://book.douban.com/subject/27174130/" data-url="https://book.douban.com/subject/27174130/"><span>《北野武的小酒馆》</span></a></p><span></span><p><a href="https://book.douban.com/subject/3369793/" data-url="https://book.douban.com/subject/3369793/"><span>《亲爱的安德烈》</span></a></p><span></span><p><a href="https://book.douban.com/subject/26319730/" data-url="https://book.douban.com/subject/26319730/"><span>《娱乐至死》</span></a></p><span></span><p><a href="https://book.douban.com/subject/1005325/" data-url="https://book.douban.com/subject/1005325/"><span>《童年的消逝》</span></a></p><span></span><p><span>A person who likes to read freely and independently is the most difficult to be conquered, which is the true meaning of reading — spiritual autonomy.</span></p><span></span><p><span>The great books are read because they have been read — They form a sort of social glue.</span></p><span></span><p><strong><span>【找到我们】</span></strong></p><span></span><p><span>同名id：穿过隧道</span></p><span></span><p><span>喜马拉雅、QQ音乐、网易云音乐、苹果播客</span></p><span></span><p><span>公众号：穿过隧道Through the Tunnel</span></p><span></span><p><span>我们播客的邮箱地址：</span></p><span></span><p><span>through_the_tunnel@outlook.com</span></p><span></span><p><span>同时非常欢迎大家在 </span><a href="https://afdian.net/@Through_the_Tunnel" data-url="https://afdian.net/@Through_the_Tunnel"><span>爱发电</span></a><span> 上支持我们！</span></p><span></span><p><span><a data-url="https://afdian.net/@Through_the_Tunnel" href="https://afdian.net/@Through_the_Tunnel">afdian.net</a></span></p>]]></description>
